    scope: "For internal DHS and DSD staff who make or shape decisions that reach other people’s lives: policy, program and operations staff, for whom this is a useful place to start in this area; quality, compliance and performance staff, who will find the deeper material here; leaders, supervisors and managers; contracts, grants and procurement staff; data, research, evaluation and analytics staff; communications, training and learning-design staff; community engagement staff; administrative and support staff. Four short lessons you can take in any order and return to. Voluntary and self-directed: no score, no ranking, no badge, no completion requirement, and nothing you write in a reflection is collected or seen. You are never asked to disclose your own identity, beliefs or personal experiences. This is not direct-service or provider training, and completion here does not count toward DHS-required training credits unless management, a director, or DHS leadership expressly approves an exception.",
