    introTranscript: "Some decisions in this work cannot be settled by looking up the rule, because more than one thing the division is genuinely obliged to protect is in play at the same time: a person’s authority over their own life, their safety, what the law requires, what the money allows, what quality oversight can actually verify, and whether the result lands the same way on everyone. It never does. This module is about that kind of decision. It gives you a way to name the obligations pulling against each other, to see the decision from standpoints other than your own, to test a reason before it hardens into a rule for everyone, and to write down seven lines that let a decision be explained, challenged and revisited later. There is no score here, and nothing you write in a reflection is collected.",
